# 7. Functional Requirements

## FR-001 — AI Assistant

The system shall provide an AI assistant accessible from Salesforce.

Example:

```text
Agent:
"Summarize this Case."
```

The assistant shall return a concise Case summary.

---

## FR-002 — Case Summary

The system shall retrieve relevant Case information and generate a summary.

The summary may include:

- Customer issue.
- Case history.
- Previous interactions.
- Current status.
- Relevant actions.
- Recommended next step.

---

## FR-003 — Case Classification

The system shall provide AI recommendations for:

```text
Category
Subcategory
Priority
Sentiment
Routing
```

---

## FR-004 — Sentiment Analysis

The system shall analyze customer communication and classify sentiment.

Supported values:

```text
Positive
Neutral
Negative
Critical
```

---

## FR-005 — Customer Profile

The assistant shall retrieve authorized customer information.

Potential information:

- Account.
- Contact.
- Customer segment.
- Active Cases.
- Previous Cases.
- Orders.
- Assets.

---

## FR-006 — Case History

The assistant shall retrieve relevant historical Cases for an authorized customer.

---

## FR-007 — Knowledge Search

The assistant shall search approved enterprise Knowledge sources.

---

## FR-008 — Knowledge Recommendation

The assistant shall recommend relevant Knowledge Articles based on Case context.

Each recommendation should provide:

- Article title.
- Relevance score where available.
- Short explanation.
- Reference/link.

---

## FR-009 — Response Generation

The system shall generate a draft response using approved context.

The response should consider:

- Customer issue.
- Case details.
- Relevant knowledge.
- Business rules.
- Communication tone.

---

## FR-010 — Human Review

AI-generated customer responses shall be presented for agent review before sending.

Possible actions:

```text
Approve
Edit
Reject
Regenerate
```

---

## FR-011 — Order Status

Where an approved external integration is available, the assistant shall retrieve order information.

Example:

```text
Agent:
"What's the status of order 100012?"

AI:
"Order 100012 was shipped on October 3 and is
currently in transit."
```

---

## FR-012 — Follow-Up Task

The system may create a Salesforce Task after authorization.

---

## FR-013 — Case Escalation

The system may recommend escalation based on business rules and AI analysis.

Actual escalation shall require the appropriate authorization.

---

# 8. AI Tool Requirements

The AI Tool Catalog shall provide controlled tool definitions.

Initial tools:

```text
getCustomerProfile
getCustomerCases
getCaseDetails
summarizeCase
classifyCase
analyzeSentiment
searchKnowledge
recommendKnowledge
generateCustomerResponse
getOrderStatus
createFollowUpTask
escalateCase
```

Each tool shall define:

```text
Tool Name
Description
Input Schema
Output Schema
Required Parameters
Allowed Values
Authorization
Execution Method
Error Handling
```

---

# 9. Tool Execution Requirements

The system shall not allow unrestricted AI-generated code or arbitrary Salesforce operations.

Tool execution shall follow:

```text
User Request
    ↓
Intent Detection
    ↓
Tool Selection
    ↓
Tool Validation
    ↓
Parameter Validation
    ↓
Authorization
    ↓
Execution
    ↓
Output Validation
    ↓
Response
```

---

# 10. RAG Requirements

The system shall support Retrieval-Augmented Generation for enterprise knowledge.

RAG sources may include:

- Salesforce Knowledge.
- Product documentation.
- FAQs.
- Support documentation.
- Approved internal documents.

The system shall prioritize trusted sources.

AI responses should be grounded in retrieved context where applicable.

---

# 11. Security Requirements

## SEC-001 — Authentication

Only authenticated Salesforce users shall access the AI Tool.

## SEC-002 — Authorization

Tool execution shall verify user permissions.

## SEC-003 — CRUD/FLS

Salesforce object and field permissions shall be respected.

## SEC-004 — Record-Level Security

The system shall respect Salesforce sharing and record visibility.

## SEC-005 — External Authentication

External APIs shall use secure authentication mechanisms.

## SEC-006 — Secret Management

Secrets shall not be hard-coded.

## SEC-007 — Sensitive Data

Sensitive information shall not be unnecessarily exposed to the AI model or application logs.

---

# 12. Non-Functional Requirements

## NFR-001 — Performance

Normal AI interactions should provide a responsive user experience.

Performance targets should be finalized during implementation and measured separately for:

- Salesforce retrieval.
- RAG retrieval.
- AI model processing.
- External API calls.
- Total response time.

---

## NFR-002 — Availability

The solution should be designed to tolerate temporary failures of dependent services.

---

## NFR-003 — Scalability

The architecture shall support increasing:

- Users.
- Cases.
- AI requests.
- Tool executions.
- Knowledge documents.

---

## NFR-004 — Maintainability

Business configuration should be externalized where appropriate using Salesforce metadata.

---

## NFR-005 — Observability

The solution shall provide monitoring and logging for:

- AI requests.
- Tool execution.
- Errors.
- Integration failures.
- Performance.

---

## NFR-006 — Auditability

Important AI-assisted actions shall be traceable.

---

# 13. Business Rules

## BRULE-001

AI recommendations shall not automatically override Salesforce business rules.

## BRULE-002

AI-generated customer communication shall require human review where configured by the business.

## BRULE-003

Users shall only access information they are authorized to access.

## BRULE-004

Only registered tools in the Tool Catalog may be executed.

## BRULE-005

Tool parameters shall be validated before execution.

## BRULE-006

High-risk operations shall require explicit confirmation or additional authorization.

